---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>wc-inline-edit</code> shows a record's value as text with a pencil button. Clicking the
  text or the button opens an editor; <kbd>Enter</kbd> saves, <kbd>Escape</kbd> cancels, and
  moving focus away saves too, so nothing typed is lost. The text takes the font of its
  surroundings, so it works in a heading.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='width: 100%; max-width: 480px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem;'>
    <h2 style='margin: 0;'>
      <wc-inline-edit id='inline-edit-title' label='Title' value='Quarterly report' required></wc-inline-edit>
    </h2>
    <wc-inline-edit
      label='Description'
      multiline
      maxlength='500'
      placeholder='Add a description'
    ></wc-inline-edit>
  </div>
  <script is:inline>
    document.querySelector('#inline-edit-title').addEventListener('change', function (event) {
      myConsole.log('change: ' + event.detail.value);
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<p>
  With <code>multiline</code> the editor is a <code>wc-textarea</code>: <kbd>Enter</kbd> starts a
  new line and <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Enter</kbd> (<kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>Enter</kbd>) saves.
  <code>show-actions</code> adds Save and Cancel buttons after the editor.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='width: 100%; max-width: 480px;'>
    <wc-inline-edit label='Owner' value='Ada Lovelace' show-actions></wc-inline-edit>
  </div>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Not a form field</h3>
<p>
  Inline edit is for records that the app saves at once. It is not form-associated and has no
  <code>name</code>. For values submitted together, use <code>wc-input</code> or
  <code>wc-textarea</code> inside a <code>wc-form</code>.
</p>
